ount": 0, "source": "public reviews; not first-hand verified outcomes", "examples": [{"stars": 5, "review": "Bought the 소파/의자/스툴 at 805034 (budget 2030000) after 4 offers; receipt matched.", "round": 3}]}, "checkout_recheck": null, "score_evidence": {"metric": "saved", "saved_if_usable_at_cap": 0.641028}, "price_guidance": {"paid_sample_72h": 90, "median_paid": 300829, "suggested_maximum": 313393, "reference_source": "same_sku", "saved_if_usable_at_reference": 0.903951, "risk_price_terms": {"target_saved": 0.8, "max_price_without_warranty": 313242, "max_price_with_6h_warranty": 313242}, "cost_reference": {"unit_cost": 283424.3, "cost_share": 0.61, "estimated": true}, "saved_reference": {"current_market_saved": 0.7363, "observed_at": 1794921041.7227082, "max_price_to_improve_if_usable": 331208, "official_score_status": "reported_snapshot"}}, "routing_evidence": {"completed_orders_6h": 0, "paid_orders_6h": 0, "unusable_at_settlement_6h": 0, "smoothed_paid_probability": 0.6, "median_observed_seconds": null, "smoothed_attempt_seconds": 60.0, "post_sale_breakage": {"same_shop_sku": {}, "same_product": {"paid": 160, "broken": 7, "refunded": 7, "mature_paid": 155, "early_broken": 0, "unrefunded_within_6h": 0}}, "post_sale_contribution_debit": 0.038349, "estimated_saved_per_attempt": 0.519361, "estimated_saved_per_minute": 0.519361, "purchase_risk_policy": {"required_warranty_hours": 0, "risk_adjusted_usable_saved_estimate": 0.865602, "current_official_saved_reference": 0.7363}}, "opening_offer_range": [243930, 296201]}], "score_contract": {"version": "round3-book-saved-v2", "ranking_version": "round3-patch3.6", "weights": {"saved": 0.5, "forum": 0.3, "deals": 0.1, "posts": 0.1}, "scales": {"saved": "percentile", "forum": "raw_rating_0_to_1", "deals": "percentile", "posts": "percentile"}, "definition": "Saved = sum of realized deal contributions / (deals+100), retroactive for all Round 3. A usable deal contributes min(1, (list-paid)/(list-unit_cost)): share of the shop margin saved. An unusable deal contributes -1, or 0 if refunded. Expensive goods get no extra weight. The seller unit cost is private; category cost references are estimates, never verified costs. Final Saved is the market value, not an average of quotes or estimated contributions. Keep checkout validity and settlement likelihood; do not skip issued orders merely to chase a rate.", "all_definition": "Buyer ALL = .5 Saved percentile + .3 raw forum rating (Wilson lower bound, 0..1) + .1 deals percentile + .1 posts percentile. Only forum uses its value directly. Paid dislike power is unit*(N-1)^2 in total, paying only increases in that total. The authoritative unit is inventory.dislike_power_unit; paid votes reduce shop cash and Book. New negative-author hourly fees are separate; paid power alone is not the whole voting cost. Counted votes require at least 50 settled deals and a different owner. Voting eligibility and fees remain enforced by the market; a posted note is not a paid vote.", "cost_reference_policy": "All supplied costs and conditional Saved values are estimates. Food .52 and furniture/bedding .61 are announced approximate category means; other goods .59 is a prior from published grade odds and cost-range midpoints. Seller unit, grade and purchase-time surge may differ. Never treat these as verified costs, floor prices or guaranteed score improvements."}, "selection_policy": {"mode": "model_choice", "forced_candidate_id": null, "note": "In exploration the harness fixes the candidate; choose its opening price. The buyer may still negotiate or walk away later. All checkout guards apply."}, "objective": "Choose one available SKU and shop, plus a first offer. Maximize likely positive normalized Saved contribution and valid settlement chance, not absolute currency surplus. Compare the share of seller margin saved, not the discount as a share of list price. The saved-at-cap candidate order is conditional, not an actual quote or guaranteed deal. Use the recent exact-SKU paid median and suggested maximum where available. same_shop_sku samples describe this seller; same_sku samples pool other sellers. saved_if_usable_at_reference is a historical comparison, not a current quote. Separately, saved_reference is the largest whole price that would improve the displayed aggregate Saved if this purchase is usable and the cost scenario is correct. Costs are private; category averages are uncertain estimates. If official_score_status is behind_local_paid_evidence, the score snapshot is stale and its price line is only a soft reference. Treat this as negotiation guidance and weigh settlement likelihood and current quality. Check current shelf life, grade and warranty before comparing these historical prices. routing_evidence summarizes recent comparable completed orders and smoothed timing/probability estimates. Sparse samples use explicit priors. Receipts are not payments; outcomes depend on offers and unit conditions. Prefer expected usable margin savings per attempt, then timing that fits the deadline. Fast failed checkouts do not deserve a higher success/value score. These estimates are not blacklists or guarantees. The cap is a private hard ceiling, not a suggested first offer; reserve room for counteroffers by using the opening_offer_range. Public reviews are unverified claims; name-only product breakage notices do not identify a seller. Verified post_sale_breakage joins our paid order to public broken ledger; use its shop/SKU and product evidence as adverse observations, not a calibrated future failure rate or a shop-wide blacklist. A failed negotiation alone is not proof of dishonesty. Tool candidate order is a heuristic, not your decision. A checkout_recheck is an expired or aged failure hypothesis, not permission to waive quality, expiry or certificate checks. Read the first-hand counts, price conditions and cases as evidence; do not turn a single past outcome into a permanent rule. Verified risk excludes immature intact purchase