ntributes -1, or 0 if refunded. Expensive goods get no extra weight. The seller unit cost is private; category cost references are estimates, never verified costs. Final Saved is the market value, not an average of quotes or estimated contributions. Keep checkout validity and settlement likelihood; do not skip issued orders merely to chase a rate.", "all_definition": "Buyer ALL = .5 Saved percentile + .3 raw forum rating (Wilson lower bound, 0..1) + .1 deals percentile + .1 posts percentile. Only forum uses its value directly. Paid dislike power is unit*(N-1)^2 in total, paying only increases in that total. The authoritative unit is inventory.dislike_power_unit; paid votes reduce shop cash and Book. New negative-author hourly fees are separate; paid power alone is not the whole voting cost. Counted votes require at least 50 settled deals and a different owner. Voting eligibility and fees remain enforced by the market; a posted note is not a paid vote.", "cost_reference_policy": "All supplied costs and conditional Saved values are estimates. Food .52 and furniture/bedding .61 are announced approximate category means; other goods .59 is a prior from published grade odds and cost-range midpoints. Seller unit, grade and purchase-time surge may differ. Never treat these as verified costs, floor prices or guaranteed score improvements."}, "selection_policy": {"mode": "model_choice", "forced_candidate_id": null, "note": "In exploration the harness fixes the candidate; choose its opening price. The buyer may still negotiate or walk away later. All checkout guards apply."}, "objective": "Choose one available SKU and shop, plus a first offer. Maximize likely positive normalized Saved contribution and valid settlement chance, not absolute currency surplus. Compare the share of seller margin saved, not the discount as a share of list price. The saved-at-cap candidate order is conditional, not an actual quote or guaranteed deal. Use the recent exact-SKU paid median and suggested