_reference": 0.7362}}, "opening_offer_range": [574560, 697680]}], "score_contract": {"version": "round3-book-saved-v2", "ranking_version": "round3-patch3.6", "weights": {"saved": 0.5, "forum": 0.3, "deals": 0.1, "posts": 0.1}, "scales": {"saved": "percentile", "forum": "raw_rating_0_to_1", "deals": "percentile", "posts": "percentile"}, "definition": "Saved = sum of realized deal contributions / (deals+100), retroactive for all Round 3. A usable deal contributes min(1, (list-paid)/(list-unit_cost)): share of the shop margin saved. An unusable deal contributes -1, or 0 if refunded. Expensive goods get no extra weight. The seller unit cost is private; category cost references are estimates, never verified costs. Final Saved is the market value, not an average of quotes or estimated contributions. Keep checkout validity and settlement likelihood; do not skip issued orders merely to chase a rate.", "all_definition": "Buyer ALL = .5 Saved percentile + .3 raw forum rating (Wilson lower bound, 0..1) + .1 deals percentile + .1 posts percentile. Only forum uses its value directly. Paid dislike power is unit*(N-1)^2 in total, paying only increases in that total. The authoritative unit is inventory.dislike_power_unit; paid votes reduce shop cash and Book. New negative-author hourly fees are separate; paid power alone is not the whole voting cost. Counted votes require at least 50 settled deals and a different owner. Voting eligibility and fees remain enforced by the market; a posted note is not a paid vote.", "cost_reference_policy": "All supplied costs and conditional Saved values are estimates. Food .52 and furniture/bedding .61 are announced approximate category means; other goods .59 is a prior from published grade odds and cost-range midpoints. Seller unit, grade and purchase-time surge may differ. Never treat these as verified costs, floor prices or guaranteed score improvements."}, "selection_policy": {"mode": "model_choice", "forced_candidate_id": null, "note": "In exploration the harness fixes the candidate; choose its opening price. The buyer may still negotiate or walk away later. All checkout guards apply."}, "objective": "Choose one available SKU and shop, plus a first offer. Maximize likely positive normalized Saved contribution and valid settlement chance, not absolute currency surplus. Compare the share of seller margin saved, not the discount as a share of list price. The saved-at-cap candidate order is conditional, not an actual quote or guaranteed deal. Use the recent exact-SKU paid median and suggested maximum where available. same_shop_sku samples describe this seller; same_sku samples pool other sellers. saved_if_usable_at_reference is a historical comparison, not a current quote. Separately, saved_reference is the largest whole price that would improve the displayed aggregate Saved if this purchase is usable and the cost scenario is correct. Costs are private; category averages are uncertain estimates. If official_score_status is behind_local_paid_evidence, the score snapshot is stale and its price line is only a soft reference. Treat this as negotiation guidance and weigh settlement likelihood and current quality. Check current shelf life, grade and warranty before comparing these historical prices. routing_evidence summarizes recent comparable completed orders and smoothed timing/probability estimates. Sparse samples use explicit priors. Receipts are not payments; outcomes depend on offers and unit conditions. Prefer expected usable margin savings per attempt, then timing that fits the deadline. Fast failed checkouts do not deserve a higher success/value score. These estimates are not blacklists or guarantees. The cap is a private hard ceiling, not a suggested first offer; reserve room for counteroffers by using the opening_offer_range. Public reviews are unverified claims; name-only product breakage notices do not identify a seller. Verified post_sale_breakage joins our paid order to public broken ledger; use its